-- The worldserver loads the players' client Spell.dbc, and a `spell_dbc` row replaces the client spell with the same
-- ID. 643 serverside rows covered spells the CoA client defines itself; their client definitions apply again.
-- 114 rows stay: 111 client rows have no effects, or fewer than the server row, and cannot run the mechanic, and
-- three scripts hook an aura type only the server row has (Garr and Majordomo Separation Anxiety, Infernal scaling).

-- Three AzerothCore mechanics used IDs the client assigns to different spells. They move to 4000000-4000002, a
-- range the client leaves unused: 100102 arena gear scaling and 100101 the Twin Val'kyr ball dummy (both "Holy
-- Light" in the client), and 43360 the Zul'Aman Fixate ("Call of the Beast" in the client).
DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (4000000, 4000001, 4000002);
